  "description": "Open spatial data for Wales, mirrored from DataMapWales (Map Data Cymru), the Welsh Government's spatial data portal: the administrative, electoral and Senedd boundaries, the census small-area geographies with deprivation, Welsh language and rural-urban statistics, Natural Resources Wales flood and water framework mapping, the LANDMAP landscape character survey, Cadw's designated historic assets and the Royal Commission's historic administrative boundaries. Every dataset is published under the Open Government Licence v3.0, evidenced per record from the portal's own ISO 19139 metadata.\n\n**Disclaimer:** a demonstration of Portolan as cloud-native infrastructure for disseminating open geodatasets. This catalog republishes data from its original publishers in cloud-native formats such as GeoParquet and PMTiles, with STAC metadata \u2014 open, standards-based and freely accessible to everyone. It is not an official service of the original publishers, which remain the authoritative source.",
